-- title:
--   Eisenstein-primary projectors on q^m-torsion, compatible in m
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be natural numbers, each assumed prime, and suppose that for every $m$ the $q^m$-torsion subgroup $\{x : q^m x = 0\}$ of $J :=$ `JZero p` is finite, where `JZero p` is the group of degree-zero divisor classes (degree-zero divisors modulo principal divisors) of the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Equip $J$ with the module structure `heckeModuleBar p` over `HeckeAlg` $= \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Nat.Primes}\ \mathbb Z$, the polynomial ring on the primes acting through the Hecke operators on $J$ (with a degenerate fallback action if those operators are not known to commute). Then there is a family $t : \mathbb N \to$ `HeckeAlg` such that for every $m$ and every $x \in J$ with $(q^m : \mathbb Z) \cdot x = 0$: (i) $t_m \cdot (t_m \cdot x) = t_m \cdot x$; (ii) $t_m \cdot x = x$ holds exactly when $x$ lies in `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`, i.e. $x$ is killed by $q^m$ and lies in $\bigsqcup_k$ of the submodules annihilated by the $k$-th power of `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, the contraction along `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal generated by $q$; and (iii) $t_{m+1} \cdot x = t_m \cdot x$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-module-theoretic core of the construction of the Eisenstein-primary projector on the $q$-power torsion of $J_0(p)$: on each $q^m$-torsion group a single Hecke element acts as an idempotent whose fixed points are precisely the $\mathfrak P$-primary part for the mod-$q$ Eisenstein maximal ideal, and these elements may be chosen to agree as $m$ grows. It feeds the scheme-theoretic statement [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronIdentityComponent.exists_heckeAlg_tower_idempotent_schemeKer_of_ringHom_of_sectionsEquiv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronIdentityComponent.exists_heckeAlg_tower_idempotent_schemeKer_of_ringHom_of_sectionsEquiv).
